        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 52.611,
        "asr_text": "Together, these studies show two different parts of the same story. An alert can disturb the moment, and nearby phone can shape the moment before it. This does not mean every person is affected in the same way outside these study settings, but it does show why 'I never checked my phone' is not the whole story. Daily reports show why this matters. In a 2018 survey of U.S. teens aged 13 to 17, 72% said they often or sometimes checked messages or notifications soon after waking. About four in 10 said they felt anxious, upset, or lonely when their phone was not nearby. A majority also felt they needed to reply quickly. The report described this as a hard-to-resist habit, not a medical diagnosis.",
        "asr_text_length": 700,
        "max_len": 751,
        "substring_ok": null,
        "length_ok": true,
        "phonetic_verdict": null,
